<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian Budget-Treasury fiscal projections.</title>
<headline>Australian Budget-Treasury fiscal projections.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Treasury on Tuesday published the following fiscal projections in the budget papers for the year to June 1998, in A$:</p>
<p>		  Underlying Chg  Revenue  Chg   Underlying Balance</p>
<p>		  Spending   pct	     pct</p>
<p>		  (A$ bln)	 (A$ bln)	 (A$ bln)    pct GDP</p>
<p>    1995/96    131.96   +3.9   121.69  +7.2   -10.27     -2.1</p>
<p>    1996/97    136.48   +1.1   129.63  +4.1    -6.86     -1.3</p>
<p>    1997/98    137.20   -1.4   133.35  +0.9    -3.85     -0.7</p>
<p>    1999/00    140.79   +0.1   142.38  +4.1    +1.60     +0.3</p>
<p>    2000/01    144.95   +0.5   150.33  +3.1    +5.38     +0.9</p>
<p>    2001/02    148.22   -0.2   158.91  +3.1   +10.69     +1.6</p>
<p>NOTE: Percentage changes are real. Figures for 1995/96 are actual, 1996/97 are estimates. For subsequent years they are projections on a no-policy change basis</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730  </p>
